# mLRS corrections and telemetry link (SERIAL7 -> RadioMaster RP4TD on mLRS)
#   why the link exists      docs/rtk-corrections-path.md, "Direction (2026-10-27)"
#   the pads                 docs/rekon10/flight-platform.md, "Serial ports"
#
# RP4TD flashed rx-radiomaster-rp4td-2400 (mLRS v1.4.04), its TX/RX pads on R7/T7. The ground
# end is a RadioMaster Ranger on mLRS, USB-C into the attic host. RTCM comes up this link;
# telemetry goes down it to the attic tlog.
#
# Proto 2 = MAVLink2. 57600 is the receiver's default "Rx Ser Baudrate"; it is ~5.8 kB/s on
# the wire against ~2 kB/s over the air in 31 Hz mode.  provenance: 2026-11-01
SERIAL7_PROTOCOL,2
SERIAL7_BAUD,57
#
# MAVLink channels are numbered in SERIALn order over the MAVLink ports. With SERIAL7 on
# protocol 2 this link is MAV4 (SERIAL0 = MAV1, SERIAL4 = MAV2, SERIAL6 = MAV3); SERIAL9 (OTG)
# moves from MAV4 to MAV5.
#
# Downlink: the four groups the ELRS link carries at 2 Hz (EXT_STAT = SYS_STATUS + GPS_RAW,
# POSITION = global/local position, EXTRA1 = ATTITUDE, EXTRA2 = VFR_HUD), EXTRA3 (battery, EKF
# status, vibration and the rest of that group) and RC_CHAN (RC_CHANNELS + SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW,
# so a radio switch can annotate the ground log) at 1 Hz. The receiver's RADIO_STATUS
# ("Rx Snd RadioStat" = ardu_1) drives ArduPilot's flow control on this channel
# (GCS_Common.cpp handle_radio_status: txbuf < 50 slows the streams), so an oversubscribed
# link slows the streams rather than overflowing.
#
# Budget. mLRS 31 Hz mode is one frame each way every 32 ms with 82 B of serial payload down
# and 64 B up (mLRS frame_types.h, setup.h): 2560 B/s down, 2000 B/s up at full link quality.
# Wire bytes per 1 Hz tick of each group, measured on the coordinator tlog of 2026-10-27
# (all groups at 2 Hz there): EXT_STAT 202, POSITION 76, EXTRA1 131, EXTRA2 31,
# EXTRA3 229, RC_CHAN 78; HEARTBEAT 21 B/s. The rates below come to ~1210 B/s, 47% of the
# downlink.  provenance: 2026-11-01
MAV4_EXT_STAT,2
MAV4_POSITION,2
MAV4_EXTRA1,2
MAV4_EXTRA2,2
MAV4_EXTRA3,1
MAV4_RC_CHAN,1
MAV4_ADSB,0
MAV4_PARAMS,0
MAV4_RAW_CTRL,0
MAV4_RAW_SENS,0
#
# 6 = bit 1 NO_FORWARD + bit 2 NOSTREAMOVERRIDE (GCS.h, enum class Option).
#   NO_FORWARD: the same reason as MAV3_OPTIONS in rc-modes.param -- without it the FC relays
#   the coordinator's broadcast VIO messages onto the radio, measured at 46% of the ELRS
#   downlink on 260812 (coordinator #197), and relays the incoming RTCM onto the other links.
#   A private channel still processes its own traffic locally, RTCM included.
#   NOSTREAMOVERRIDE: ignore REQUEST_DATA_STREAM, so a GCS on this link cannot set and save
#   the rates above (Mission Planner did that to MAV3 on 2026-10-24).
#   provenance: 2026-11-01
MAV4_OPTIONS,6
